Great — starting with **Backend + LLD (Low Level Design)** is exactly how real production systems are built.
I’ll design this like a scalable MERN + AI microservice system (the kind interviewers love).

Below is a **complete Backend LLD** you can directly turn into code.

---

# 📐 Backend Low Level Design (LLD)

AI Plant Health Monitoring System

---

## 🏗 System Architecture (Microservice-ready)

```
Mobile App (React Native)
        |
        v
API Gateway (Express)
        |
-------------------------------------------------
|            |              |                  |
Auth Service  Plant Service  Scan Service   AI Service (Python)
        |
     MongoDB Atlas
```

---

# 📁 Backend Folder Structure (Node + Express)

```
backend/
│
├── src/
│   ├── app.js
│   ├── server.js
│
│   ├── config/
│   │   ├── db.js
│   │   ├── env.js
│
│   ├── routes/
│   │   ├── auth.routes.js
│   │   ├── plant.routes.js
│   │   ├── scan.routes.js
│
│   ├── controllers/
│   │   ├── auth.controller.js
│   │   ├── plant.controller.js
│   │   ├── scan.controller.js
│
│   ├── services/
│   │   ├── ai.service.js
│   │   ├── upload.service.js
│
│   ├── models/
│   │   ├── User.js
│   │   ├── Plant.js
│   │   ├── ScanHistory.js
│
│   ├── middlewares/
│   │   ├── auth.middleware.js
│   │   ├── error.middleware.js
│
│   └── utils/
│       ├── jwt.js
│       ├── response.js
│
└── package.json
```

